<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ordenações Afonsinas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1446">1446</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Afonsine Ordinances</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ordenações Afonsinas were the first general code of Portuguese law, completed around 1446 in the reign of Afonso V, after whom they are named. In five books they gathered royal laws, customs and rules from Roman and canon law. They were replaced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manueline-style">Manueline</a> Ordinances under Manuel I and the Philippine Ordinances of 1603, which stayed in force in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> until 1916.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ordenacoes-afonsinas.jpg" alt="Ordenações Afonsinas" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N%C3%BAcleo_Antigo_C%C3%B3dice_14,_book_V,_folio_1_(recto).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
